#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184007 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc8dc1a1-9606-5b67-942e-219ab2ddfc1c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Nilpotent Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "61a0b8a7-332d-5ae1-ad46-a65369bc87d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4415" :question/problem "Find $B^2$ given that $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Computing $B^2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB^{2} &= B \\cdot B \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= O\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since $B^2=O$, the matrix $B$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184008 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b51e8ff1-247b-5efd-a684-8fca6c064e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of an Idempotent Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "906ff9b7-c304-5b9a-b152-cef3bf343de1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4416" :question/problem "Find $C^5$ given that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute $C^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nC^{2} &= C \\cdot C \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $C^2=C$, so $C$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute $C^5$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nC^{5} &= C^{2} \\cdot C^{2} \\cdot C \\\\\n&= C \\cdot C \\cdot C \\\\\n&= C^{2} \\cdot C \\\\\n&= C \\cdot C \\\\\n&= C^{2} \\\\\n&= C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b51e8ff1-247b-5efd-a684-8fca6c064e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of an Idempotent Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85718515-480f-51ed-871c-e22890c5e6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 27 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183138} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c70f31-301d-5eec-ad41-9b27fba32a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183139} {:answer/id #uuid "5380696b-843e-5d90-9278-4659cd526c8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183140} {:answer/id #uuid "613ca3b6-8843-505f-bbc0-db80dd0c4042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 18 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183141} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5f3459-97fc-5db6-bcbf-a5cf4009befe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c70f31-301d-5eec-ad41-9b27fba32a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183139} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e387ce5-0d2e-594a-8997-284fa7af81e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183137}] :question/id #uuid "122c0975-4dfe-5f37-a6e1-cdeef5051652" :qu